maya: Heads up — hitting a weird one with JSON mode + function/tool calling in the JS SDK. When the request triggers an auth retry (401 -> refresh token -> retry) the JSON-mode helper sometimes returns an empty object instead of the parsed structured output. Repro attached.

ash: Can you paste a tiny repro? which SDK version? :thinking_face:

maya: repro (JS, sdk@0.23.1):
```js
const client = new RedwoodSDK({ jsonMode: true });

const res = await client.callFunction('order.lookup', { orderId: '123' }, {
  schema: { type: 'object', properties: { items: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { id: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['id'] } } }, required: ['items'] }
});

// When the access token expired the first try returns 401, client refreshes and retries.
// Expected: res.parsed.items = [{ id: 'abc' }]
// Observed: res.parsed === {}  // empty object
```

sam: hmm — does the raw text body include the JSON on retry? Could be we skip parse on the retry path. Add a quick `console.log(response.text)` in the SDK around the retry hook.

maya: I logged it — the retried response has the correct JSON payload. It seems the JSON-mode parsing helper short-circuits if a prior attempt set an internal flag during the auth error.

lia: Possible call path: auth -> error handler sets `hadAuthError = true`, then retry returns but we early-return from parse because of that flag. I saw something similar in the Python SDK last month. Workaround: for now disable `jsonMode` or do manual JSON.parse on `res.raw` after call.

maya: workaround works. Still pretty annoying for onboarding/sample apps where folks expect structured outputs out of the box. Can someone take a quick look in the JS helper flow?

devex-bot: Issue created: github.com/redwood-inference/sdk-js/issues/1287 — "JS SDK: jsonMode parsing skipped after auth retry (function call)" by maya. Tagging eng and devex. :ticket:

ash: I'll pick this up — adding to my queue. Quick patch idea: reset the parse guard before executing parse on retried responses.

sam: also double-check streaming case — similar guard could drop buffered chunks.

lia: added a unit test suggestion in the issue for auth-retry + functioncall + schema validate.

maya: thanks all :thumbsup: will update the sample app doc to mention the temp workaround until the patch ships.
